# CODEOWNERS for go-z-ai.
# https://docs.github.com/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Today this is a single-maintainer project, so every path routes to @SamyRai.
# The file exists so that (a) GitHub surfaces the right reviewer automatically
# once collaborators join, and (b) the main-branch ruleset can later flip on
# `require_code_owner_review` for PRs touching the public API surface without
# further config changes.
#
# When regular outside contributors arrive: add them under the paths they own
# (e.g. `/# TUI  @contributor-a` above the catch-all). The catch-all stays.

# Public API surface — the semver contract. Any change here deserves a
# maintainer review even once domain-specific paths are delegated.
/pkg/          @SamyRai

# Release-critical config — gating, signing, attestation.
/.github/      @SamyRai
/.goreleaser.yml @SamyRai
/Makefile      @SamyRai
/go.mod        @SamyRai

# Catch-all: everything else (CLI, TUI, sitegen, docs, examples).
*              @SamyRai
